1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,452
A language model must pick the next word. Here it has four candidates:

2
00:00:04,552 --> 00:00:05,924
cat, dog, fox, and owl.

3
00:00:06,024 --> 00:00:10,443
The model gives each candidate a score. The score is called a logit.

4
00:00:10,543 --> 00:00:12,107
Cat has the highest logit.

5
00:00:12,201 --> 00:00:15,054
Softmax turns the logits into probabilities.

6
00:00:15,154 --> 00:00:17,848
At temperature one, cat gets sixty-one percent.

7
00:00:17,934 --> 00:00:21,278
Temperature divides every logit before softmax.

8
00:00:21,378 --> 00:00:24,657
At T equal to one half, the logits move apart.

9
00:00:24,757 --> 00:00:26,470
Cat now gets eighty-four percent.

10
00:00:26,568 --> 00:00:28,140
Pause here and predict.

11
00:00:28,240 --> 00:00:31,724
When T rises to 2, does cat stay the most likely token?

12
00:00:34,818 --> 00:00:36,540
Now raise the temperature.

13
00:00:36,640 --> 00:00:39,791
At T equal to two, the logits move together.

14
00:00:39,891 --> 00:00:41,796
The probabilities become more equal.

15
00:00:41,884 --> 00:00:43,414
Why does this happen?

16
00:00:43,514 --> 00:00:47,577
The ratio of two probabilities depends only on the distance between

17
00:00:47,677 --> 00:00:51,304
their dots. A larger distance gives a larger ratio.

18
00:00:51,404 --> 00:00:54,333
A smaller distance gives a ratio closer to one.

19
00:00:54,418 --> 00:00:56,673
Why exp, and not something simpler?

20
00:00:56,773 --> 00:01:01,524
Divide each logit by their sum, and owl gets minus zero point four.

21
00:01:01,624 --> 00:01:03,858
A probability cannot be negative.

22
00:01:03,958 --> 00:01:07,302
Exp makes every weight positive and keeps the order.

23
00:01:07,402 --> 00:01:09,550
And it turns a gap into a ratio.

24
00:01:09,650 --> 00:01:12,473
That is why only the distance between the dots matters.

25
00:01:14,268 --> 00:01:18,073
At a very low temperature, the top token takes almost all the

26
00:01:18,173 --> 00:01:18,955
probability.

27
00:01:19,055 --> 00:01:22,627
At a very high temperature, every token gets almost the same

28
00:01:22,727 --> 00:01:23,350
probability.

29
00:01:23,434 --> 00:01:25,988
In every case, the order stays the same.

30
00:01:26,088 --> 00:01:29,197
Cat is always first, and owl is always last.

31
00:01:29,297 --> 00:01:31,245
Temperature changes only the spread.
